# Account System & VPN Authorization

## Project Goal
Build a complete user account + permission system that allows Alex to:
1. Send one-time invite links to people (via email)
2. They register their own passkey using the invite
3. Alex grants granular permissions (VPN locations + subdomains/sites)
4. Users login with their passkey and access only what they're allowed to reach
5. All access is logged and auditable

Current user: Dad (already invited via existing invite system)

## Architecture Overview

### Three Systems (Must Work Together)

**1. Admin Console (selfhost main app)**
- Owner-only authentication (password + Touch ID/Face ID)
- Invite minting: `selfhost people invite <name>` → one-time code
- People registry: stores who exists and their capabilities
- Located: `crates/app/admin/`

**2. Account Manager (NEW - built this session)**
- Email/password login → 24h VPN token
- Subdomain/site permission tracking
- Admin UI at localhost:3000 for granting access
- Located: `crates/services/account-manager/`
- Database: SQLite at `~/.selfhost/data/accounts.db`

**3. Secure-VPN Server (NEEDS INTEGRATION)**
- Client VPN authentication
- Permission validation (NOT YET WIRED)
- Located: separate repo `RockyWearsAHat/Secure-VPN`
- Server file: `server.py` (Python)

